WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.359 --> 00:00:08.059
How do Americans feel about Melania Trump?

00:00:08.059 --> 00:00:10.480
And what about the previous First Lady, Michelle
Obama?

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:14.809
A November poll from Quinnipiac University
provides some answers.

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:19.490
Two years into the Trump presidency, Melania
Trump is still not well known.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:23.160
In the poll of registered voters, 40 percent
said they hadn’t heard enough about her

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.160
to have an opinion.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:29.670
Of the remainder, more people had a favorable
view, 35 percent, than an unfavorable one,

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:30.970
20 percent.

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:32.910
Men and women had similar views.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:37.170
Michelle Obama, by contrast, has stayed in
the limelight since her husband left the presidency,

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.510
and she is very well known.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:44.010
In the Quinnipiac poll, only 11 percent hadn’t
heard enough about her.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:48.530
Sixty-three percent of registered voters had
a favorable opinion of her and 24 percent

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:49.880
and unfavorable one.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:54.390
Both men and women gave her high 
marks, but women were more positive than men,

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:56.630
70 to 56 percent.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:01:01.510
Mrs. Trump guards her privacy, and the polls
suggest she has been successful in doing so.

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:06.860
Even three in ten Republicans hadn’t heard
enough about Melania Trump to venture an opinion!

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:10.120
Should First ladies be involved in politics?

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:11.920
Let us know in our poll.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:16.580
Also, let us know what other topics you’d
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:20.220
and be sure to like and subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

